message: "If you use this hardware design, code, dataset or the research log, please cite it as below."
title: "TipToe: an open point-foot biped and its sim2real research log"
authors:
  - name: "jiz322"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-24
repository-code: "https://github.com/jiz322/tiptoe-biped"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - biped
  - point-foot
  - sim2real
  - reinforcement learning
  - Isaac Lab
  - open hardware
  - RobStride
abstract: >
  A 6-DOF point-foot biped built for about 5700 CNY from four RobStride RS01,
  two EL05, a Raspberry Pi 5 and printed parts, with a belt-driven knee. Trained
  with PPO in Isaac Lab and deployed through a Python CAN stack. The repository
  contains the hardware files, the training environment, the deploy stack, the
  hardware recordings, and a retrospective of every fix needed for the first
  6 s free-standing balance, built by one person working with an AI coding agent.
